WEBVTT

00:01.120 --> 00:03.440
I found out about Alan and Elena.

00:03.780 --> 00:05.810
They're the water god's children.

00:06.400 --> 00:07.530
Whee!

00:08.090 --> 00:09.950
Wait up!

00:08.090 --> 00:12.110
Where is their father now, 
and what is he doing?

00:16.160 --> 00:18.990
Okay, I get it. You can't tell me.

00:20.120 --> 00:25.100
<i>I wonder what Alan and Elena's 
father, the water god, is like...</i>

00:26.260 --> 00:29.960
<i>If this is a statue of the water 
god, I guess he looks like this?</i>

00:30.530 --> 00:34.680
<i>Syl's reaction gave me the impression 
that he's kind of gaudy.</i>

00:35.500 --> 00:39.760
<i>Of course, if he showed up now and 
took them back, I'd miss them...</i>

00:39.760 --> 00:41.390
By the way, Takumi...

00:41.640 --> 00:43.220
Congratulations!

00:44.180 --> 00:45.540
Ta-da!

00:45.540 --> 00:49.860
You are officially my disciple now!

00:49.860 --> 00:52.460
An official... disciple?

00:52.460 --> 00:57.010
It did happen a little 
sooner than I'd predicted,

00:57.010 --> 00:58.770
but, overall, I expected this!

00:58.770 --> 00:59.830
You did?

01:00.160 --> 01:03.560
Disciples become true 
disciples only when given

01:03.560 --> 01:06.180
the thing that they'll symbolize,

01:06.180 --> 01:08.750
or, in other words, a specialty 
that they're in charge of.

01:09.040 --> 01:12.670
So you're saying you'll 
be giving me work to do?

01:12.670 --> 01:15.220
Well, it's not work, exactly...

01:15.630 --> 01:18.100
You'll basically be a symbol.

01:18.100 --> 01:20.850
For example, my symbol is wind.

01:20.850 --> 01:22.430
Well, yeah. You're the god of wind.

01:22.690 --> 01:25.390
I get that, but... so what's mine, then?

01:27.690 --> 01:28.500
Syl?

01:30.320 --> 01:32.320
Nurturing and education.

01:32.660 --> 01:35.000
And why would those be my...

01:35.490 --> 01:38.780
Oh, because of Alan and Elena?

01:39.770 --> 01:42.540
But does that fall under the 
wind god's jurisdiction?

01:42.870 --> 01:45.520
I'm the disciple of the wind god, right?

01:45.520 --> 01:47.680
I thought it'd be something more... windy...

01:47.680 --> 01:52.710
Nurturing and education are the 
creator god Marianolla's domain.

01:52.710 --> 01:54.960
<i>Wait, is he </i>mad<i>?</i>

01:55.280 --> 02:01.070
I mean, that can't be helped, considering 
you've received Marianolla's blessing!

02:01.070 --> 02:06.180
But why doesn't my disciple have 
a specialty connected to wind?!

02:06.180 --> 02:10.000
I'm the one who found you, after all!

02:10.000 --> 02:12.240
More like you accidentally 
killed me...

02:14.080 --> 02:17.610
Well, not much you can do if 
that was Marianolla's choice.

02:17.850 --> 02:19.830
I know that, but...

02:20.610 --> 02:24.060
And? What am I supposed to do from now on?

02:24.060 --> 02:26.580
You can just do what you've 
been doing all this time.

02:26.580 --> 02:31.630
You're doing plenty to fulfill your 
role just by raising those kids.

02:31.630 --> 02:32.990
Really?

02:33.820 --> 02:38.300
Oh, right! I have some items for you 
from the fire god, Salamantyll!

02:41.760 --> 02:43.720
Inventory

02:42.000 --> 02:43.720
What? This many?

02:44.000 --> 02:47.600
It's to thank you for improving 
the cooking in Etelldia.

02:48.480 --> 02:51.980
Remember those dessert breads 
you made famous in Shireen?

02:52.300 --> 02:55.980
Those have spread to other 
nations now, as well.

02:56.490 --> 03:00.400
And you seasoned a dish with 
soy sauce in Bailey, right?

03:00.400 --> 03:02.760
That's going to spread like wildfire, too!

03:03.630 --> 03:06.160
Oh, the butter and soy sauce seasoning?

03:06.560 --> 03:09.370
Butter and soy sauce is yummy!

03:09.660 --> 03:12.090
You probably didn't know this,

03:12.090 --> 03:16.280
but cooking in Etelldia didn't change 
at all for several centuries.

03:16.280 --> 03:17.620
Oh, come on.

03:17.620 --> 03:19.340
It's true!

03:19.760 --> 03:21.360
I mean, maybe a few tweaks,

03:21.360 --> 03:24.300
but no new dishes were ever introduced.

03:24.660 --> 03:27.970
So the fire god is just overjoyed.

03:27.970 --> 03:30.000
Cooking is his domain, after all.

03:30.000 --> 03:31.270
Oh, really?

03:31.660 --> 03:34.840
He said he'd arrange a contracted 
beast for you too,

03:34.840 --> 03:36.980
as well as fire magic skills.

03:37.280 --> 03:41.450
Really? It'll be cool to 
be able to use fire magic.

03:41.750 --> 03:46.250
Not all monsters take a lot of 
damage from wind and water magic.

03:46.920 --> 03:49.040
Fire makes you <i>that</i> happy?

03:59.510 --> 04:05.640
<b>A Journey Through Another World: 
Raising Kids While Adventuring</b>

05:21.460 --> 05:26.470
<b>What's a Dad?</b>

05:21.890 --> 05:23.920
Okay, see you later, Syl.

05:23.920 --> 05:27.000
Well, shall we find lodging 
and turn in for the day?

05:27.000 --> 05:29.490
Yeah! Yay!

05:31.010 --> 05:32.700
That was a close one.

05:33.990 --> 05:38.060
<i>Where is their father now, 
and what is he doing?</i>

05:38.060 --> 05:40.650
I can't tell him! I just can't!

05:40.650 --> 05:43.780
I can't tell the guy who's been 
taking such good care of those kids

05:44.960 --> 05:49.490
that the water god got an Etelldia 
woman pregnant and she had twins

05:49.490 --> 05:53.710
while he's been off fooling 
with another woman!

05:54.430 --> 05:56.570
That philandering water god Wyndell!

05:56.570 --> 05:58.610
Where in the world is he?!

05:58.610 --> 05:59.700
Heya, Sylphyryll.

06:00.550 --> 06:02.520
Why the doom and gloom?

06:02.520 --> 06:05.090
Th-The fire god, Salamantyll!

06:05.370 --> 06:07.000
How long have you been here?

06:07.000 --> 06:09.130
Since you said, "That was a close one."

06:09.130 --> 06:10.720
So the whole time, then.

06:11.040 --> 06:14.060
So this... Takuya, was it? 
You give him my items?

06:14.060 --> 06:16.880
It's Takumi! And yes, I did!

06:16.880 --> 06:20.060
He was really happy about the fire 
magic, so be sure to give him some!

06:20.370 --> 06:21.600
Of course!

06:21.600 --> 06:24.780
I've got my best contracted 
beast set aside for him, too!

06:25.440 --> 06:29.540
Hang on! Your "best"? What 
are you going to give him?

06:29.540 --> 06:31.700
You'll find out when he gets it.

06:32.080 --> 06:35.660
When you get this enthusiastic, 
it never ends well.

06:36.390 --> 06:38.140
Is this going to be okay?

06:38.140 --> 06:41.420
I hope it's not something that'll 
cause Takumi too much trouble.

06:48.010 --> 06:49.400
Joule!

06:49.400 --> 06:50.690
Feat!

06:50.690 --> 06:52.720
Wait!

06:51.050 --> 06:52.720
This way!

06:52.720 --> 06:54.560
<i>Think you can catch me?</i>

06:55.240 --> 06:58.830
<i>The next day, we visited the beach again.</i>

07:00.400 --> 07:02.330
You're not going to play, Bolt?

07:02.330 --> 07:04.150
<i>No, Chief. I...</i>

07:07.390 --> 07:11.110
Now you've done it! Rawr!

07:11.680 --> 07:12.820
Okay!

07:26.300 --> 07:27.870
More! More!

07:27.870 --> 07:29.430
Okay, here it comes!

07:31.150 --> 07:33.470
Rolly roll!

07:39.110 --> 07:41.100
Again! Again!

07:41.100 --> 07:43.060
What? You still want to keep going?

07:43.310 --> 07:47.010
<i>Well, maybe it's a good chance 
to work on my water magic.</i>

07:53.930 --> 07:56.100
A l-lion?!

07:56.540 --> 07:57.660
Wait, but...

07:58.060 --> 08:00.100
Are they supposed to be this big?!

08:01.470 --> 08:02.830
Appraise.

08:03.140 --> 08:06.210
Race: Scarlet King Leo...

08:06.210 --> 08:08.090
"Takumi's contracted beast"?!

08:08.710 --> 08:11.690
He said he'd arrange a contracted 
beast for you, too...

08:12.690 --> 08:16.180
Whoa... I definitely wasn't expecting this.

08:16.410 --> 08:17.680
Wow!

08:17.680 --> 08:19.140
It's so big!

08:19.510 --> 08:24.100
Um... The fire god sent you here, right?

08:27.140 --> 08:30.730
<i>It's so big, every little noise 
it makes seems enormous.</i>

08:30.730 --> 08:33.570
<i>It doesn't appear to have 
the Telepathy skill yet.</i>

08:33.920 --> 08:35.100
Well?

08:35.100 --> 08:36.280
What's his name?

08:36.690 --> 08:38.490
Well, um...

08:39.440 --> 08:41.200
How about Vector?

08:41.200 --> 08:43.370
What do you think of "Vector" for your name?

08:49.160 --> 08:50.560
<i>I guess he likes it.</i>

08:50.560 --> 08:53.420
<i>Yeah. And he's much tamer than he seems.</i>

08:53.680 --> 08:56.250
He's definitely huge, though.

08:56.250 --> 08:58.530
He'll be great to have 
on our side in battle,

08:58.530 --> 09:00.740
but he can't walk around with us like this.

09:00.740 --> 09:03.390
Vector, sorry, but can you get smaller?

09:09.600 --> 09:11.650
Vector! Vector!

09:13.330 --> 09:15.750
You know what? I'm Alan...

09:15.750 --> 09:17.160
And I'm Elena!

09:17.530 --> 09:21.120
And I'm Takumi. Glad to meet you, Vector.

09:25.350 --> 09:28.220
Guys, Vector is one of us from now on.

09:28.220 --> 09:29.540
Be friends with him, okay?

09:29.890 --> 09:31.000
<i>Okay!</i>

09:32.720 --> 09:34.720
Here it goes, Joule!

09:34.720 --> 09:35.890
Yah!

09:40.680 --> 09:42.260
You're next, Vector!

09:42.520 --> 09:43.970
Go!

09:49.150 --> 09:51.980
Hey, Vector, where are you going?!

09:55.610 --> 09:57.450
Oh! Here he comes!

09:57.840 --> 09:59.740
He has something in his mouth.

09:59.740 --> 10:00.620
Huh?

10:00.960 --> 10:03.120
What does he have in his...

10:03.120 --> 10:04.330
What?!

10:04.740 --> 10:07.540
A p-p-p...

10:07.800 --> 10:09.910
person?!

10:12.000 --> 10:16.380
V-Vector, you're not trying to... e-eat a...

10:18.560 --> 10:21.390
A-Are you all right?! 
You're not dead, are you?!

10:23.610 --> 10:26.560
I guess she's just unconscious... or...

10:26.850 --> 10:28.020
Sleeping.

10:28.270 --> 10:29.750
Looks like it.

10:29.750 --> 10:32.610
I'm sorry. Please allow 
me to check your status.

10:33.440 --> 10:39.320
Status

10:33.440 --> 10:39.320
Name: Vivianne 
Race: Demon (Vampire) 
Job: Spy 
Level: 54 
Skills: Swordsmanship (short sword),
Throw, Dark magic, Daily-use magic,
Dismantle, Jump, Insight, Hide, Sneak,
Night Vision, Unlock, Dismantle trap,
Medicine-making, Resistance to magic attacks,
Resistance to status effects

10:33.440 --> 10:39.320
m 0 0 l 390 0 l 390 270 l 0 270

10:34.130 --> 10:36.150
Her name is Vivianne...

10:36.150 --> 10:39.320
Her race... She's a Demon?  And not only that...

10:39.320 --> 10:41.280
Status

10:39.720 --> 10:41.280
A vampire?!

10:41.920 --> 10:47.250
<i>I know that in Etelldia, demons are treated 
the same as races like elf and dwarf,</i>

10:47.520 --> 10:50.460
<i>so I don't think they have an antagonistic 
relationship with humans.</i>

10:50.720 --> 10:54.140
Vector, did you find her 
passed out over there?

10:55.130 --> 10:56.170
I see...

10:56.400 --> 10:59.200
But you shouldn't have 
dragged her like that.

10:59.200 --> 11:02.590
She could've been hurt 
if this wasn't all sand.

11:04.880 --> 11:07.300
I-I'm not angry, okay?

11:07.300 --> 11:09.480
Just be more careful next time.

11:11.120 --> 11:12.990
Poke, poke.

11:15.070 --> 11:17.570
So... hungry...

11:17.890 --> 11:18.860
Me, too!

11:18.910 --> 11:20.030
Me, too!

11:20.480 --> 11:23.490
Why don't we go ahead and have lunch, then?

11:25.690 --> 11:28.410
Guys, the food's ready!

11:28.410 --> 11:30.090
Yay!

11:28.920 --> 11:30.090
Food?!

11:32.110 --> 11:34.080
Let's eat!

11:37.670 --> 11:39.760
<i>Yum!</i>

11:47.430 --> 11:48.560
Here.

11:48.920 --> 11:50.310
I can have these?!

11:50.310 --> 11:52.560
I don't know if you'll like them, but sure.

11:53.740 --> 11:55.610
I happily accept!

12:05.040 --> 12:09.030
Whoa, now. Those are just for you 
two. You don't need to rush.

12:09.030 --> 12:10.900
Eat slowly, okay?

12:10.900 --> 12:11.870
By the way...

12:13.060 --> 12:16.680
It seemed like you passed out 
from hunger. What happened?

12:18.900 --> 12:20.840
Uh, it can wait until after you eat.

12:23.550 --> 12:25.760
Ah, I'm stuffed.

12:25.760 --> 12:27.860
Thank you for the meal!

12:27.860 --> 12:29.840
<i>She really </i>was<i> hungry...</i>

12:29.840 --> 12:30.220
Oh!

12:30.690 --> 12:32.650
My name is Vivianne.

12:32.650 --> 12:35.440
You can call me Vivianne or just Vivi.

12:35.440 --> 12:36.650
Alan!

12:36.650 --> 12:37.520
Elena!

12:37.800 --> 12:39.190
My name is Takumi.

12:39.190 --> 12:39.940
Anyway!

12:40.360 --> 12:42.660
What were those things?

12:42.660 --> 12:45.730
I've never seen anything like them before!

12:45.730 --> 12:48.210
Oh, those are called rice balls.

12:48.210 --> 12:50.120
They're made by cooking 
white wheat in water.

12:50.380 --> 12:53.750
White wheat? The stuff they 
use as livestock feed?

12:53.750 --> 12:59.130
Oh, sorry. Where I come from, 
people eat it all the time.

12:59.130 --> 13:01.210
Did I offend you?

13:01.210 --> 13:04.220
Oh, no! They were delicious, 
so it's no problem!

13:04.760 --> 13:08.730
I had no idea white wheat could 
be so delicious, though!

13:08.730 --> 13:11.080
Your big brother's a great cook, isn't he?

13:11.080 --> 13:12.720
Or wait... Is he your father?

13:13.080 --> 13:14.480
He's Taku.

13:14.480 --> 13:17.390
Ah! I guess "brother" was correct, then!

13:17.390 --> 13:20.070
He didn't react at all, though.

13:20.070 --> 13:21.690
Maybe he's their dad after all?

13:21.690 --> 13:22.820
"Brother" was right!

13:23.100 --> 13:26.960
Sorry! I just love learning 
people's secrets!

13:26.960 --> 13:29.260
I <i>am</i> a spy, after all!

13:29.260 --> 13:32.290
And why was a spy passed out over there?

13:32.290 --> 13:34.310
Well, um...

13:34.310 --> 13:38.960
Oh, that's right! I was heading 
for the town of Albaire,

13:38.960 --> 13:41.460
and I had forgotten to buy food.

13:41.870 --> 13:46.430
I stayed alive by hunting and 
picking fruits on the way,

13:46.430 --> 13:49.100
but for the past couple of 
days, pickings have been slim.

13:49.100 --> 13:53.430
You should've turned back when 
you realized you had no food!

13:53.720 --> 13:56.650
Well, I just figured it'd work out somehow!

13:56.650 --> 13:58.400
I had to make my report, anyway!

13:58.400 --> 13:59.980
Report?

13:59.980 --> 14:00.940
That's right!

14:01.290 --> 14:06.900
My mission this time was a background check 
on the man a certain noble lady's engaged to...

14:06.900 --> 14:08.990
And it turns out that man...

14:09.360 --> 14:12.870
was harboring a commoner 
girl in the mansion!

14:12.870 --> 14:13.760
Ooh!

14:13.760 --> 14:16.330
Uh, do you guys even know what that means?

14:16.640 --> 14:19.490
He didn't seem to have any 
intention of hiding her.

14:19.490 --> 14:23.730
Frankly, there was no need for me 
to infiltrate disguised as a maid.

14:23.730 --> 14:25.800
So that's why you're dressed like that.

14:26.130 --> 14:29.760
Oops! I need to go give my report!

14:29.760 --> 14:32.010
Thank you for the delicious food!

14:32.380 --> 14:33.680
Take this as thanks.

14:33.950 --> 14:35.110
What is it?

14:35.560 --> 14:36.450
Appraise.

14:37.390 --> 14:41.570
"Dew of the White Rose. 
A vampire aphrodisiac.

14:37.390 --> 14:47.400
Appraise

14:37.390 --> 14:47.400
Dew of the White Rose

14:37.390 --> 14:47.400
Dew of the Red Rose

14:41.570 --> 14:43.890
Works only on men."

14:43.890 --> 14:47.400
"Dew of the Red Rose.
A vampire aphrodisiac.

14:47.400 --> 14:49.870
Works only on women."

14:49.870 --> 14:50.990
Wait, these...

14:50.990 --> 14:54.650
Ah, it seems you know what 
sort of medicine that is.

14:54.650 --> 14:59.160
I made them. They're highly 
effective and super popular!

14:59.160 --> 15:00.390
Drinks?

15:00.390 --> 15:01.370
Can we drink them?

15:01.370 --> 15:02.190
No!

15:02.190 --> 15:04.130
Well, thanks for the food!

15:04.130 --> 15:05.250
Hey, hang on!

15:09.000 --> 15:10.280
Taku.

15:10.840 --> 15:12.160
What is it?

15:12.160 --> 15:13.800
What's a "dad"?

15:14.080 --> 15:15.010
Huh?!

15:16.170 --> 15:17.390
Well, um...

15:17.970 --> 15:19.430
Staaaaaaare

15:22.260 --> 15:26.240
Well, do you know what a father is?

15:26.240 --> 15:27.150
Nuh-uh.

15:27.150 --> 15:31.110
<i>Oh, man... They don't know 
anything about families?</i>

15:31.750 --> 15:35.450
<i>They treat me like their big brother, 
like it's natural to them.</i>

15:32.070 --> 15:33.160
Taku!

15:33.400 --> 15:34.240
Taku!

15:34.480 --> 15:35.450
Taku!

15:35.450 --> 15:40.160
<i>I was sure they knew what 
a brother was, at least.</i>

15:40.160 --> 15:44.210
Oh, out on the town with 
your big brother? How nice!

15:44.640 --> 15:47.170
<i>Maybe they understood it because 
people said things like that?</i>

15:47.520 --> 15:51.090
Um... You know what a big brother is, right?

15:51.090 --> 15:52.130
You!

15:52.130 --> 15:52.880
That's right.

15:53.310 --> 15:55.320
I'm Elena's big brother.

15:55.320 --> 15:57.100
I'm Alan's little sister.

15:57.100 --> 16:00.490
What? Really? You know that much, then...

16:00.490 --> 16:05.060
Okay, then did you know a "brother" and 
a "sister" are part of a "family"?

16:05.730 --> 16:07.130
Family?

16:09.990 --> 16:13.450
Okay, listen. Your family 
has a mom and a dad,

16:13.830 --> 16:17.160
and the two of you were born from them.

16:17.570 --> 16:18.830
Do you get that?

16:20.270 --> 16:21.830
I guess it's still too difficult...

16:22.360 --> 16:24.140
Were you born too?

16:24.140 --> 16:26.540
Yeah, I sure was.

16:26.800 --> 16:28.500
Is everyone born?

16:28.500 --> 16:29.960
That's right.

16:30.260 --> 16:32.880
Being born is a wonderful thing.

16:33.220 --> 16:35.640
Yay! Wonderful thing!

16:40.580 --> 16:42.940
"Where are our mom and dad?"

16:42.940 --> 16:45.900
I wasn't sure what I'd do 
if they asked me that,

16:46.870 --> 16:48.720
but it didn't get that far.

16:49.970 --> 16:54.600
They'll probably ask one day, 
when they're a little older.

16:55.740 --> 16:58.630
<i>The next day, to commemorate 
our arrival into town,</i>

16:58.630 --> 17:00.680
<i>we visited the guild in Bailey</i>

17:00.680 --> 17:03.420
<i>and took on a quest to gather materials.</i>

17:03.420 --> 17:05.870
We can complete this one 
with what we have on hand.

17:06.160 --> 17:08.590
Hello. Are you looking for work?

17:08.900 --> 17:12.410
No, I already have all the 
materials this one asks for,

17:12.410 --> 17:13.920
so I wanted to accept it.

17:13.920 --> 17:16.800
Oh, I'm sorry! You're an adventurer!

17:17.280 --> 17:20.000
We just got into town the other day.

17:20.000 --> 17:23.770
I see. In that case, 
I'll take your guild card.

17:25.230 --> 17:27.440
What?! Rank A?!

17:28.230 --> 17:30.220
Well, yeah...

17:30.220 --> 17:31.900
F-Forgive me!

17:32.340 --> 17:35.110
You have all the materials listed here?

17:35.110 --> 17:36.820
Yes, right here.

17:37.310 --> 17:39.530
Then I'll check them over 
and add it to your car—

17:39.530 --> 17:42.240
What?! A labyrinth?!

17:42.500 --> 17:44.960
You found a new labyrinth?!

17:45.460 --> 17:49.420
There's a labyrinth called Sazanami 
in your record of labyrinths!

17:49.760 --> 17:54.090
<i>Oh, she means the labyrinth 
we found under the ocean?</i>

17:54.090 --> 17:56.380
<i>So that was undiscovered?</i>

17:57.390 --> 17:59.970
<i>Was that... bad?</i>

18:00.540 --> 18:01.930
Um...

18:02.310 --> 18:05.390
We happened to find it while 
playing in the ocean.

18:05.390 --> 18:07.280
So it was undiscovered?

18:07.280 --> 18:10.150
Discovering a new labyrinth is a huge deal!

18:10.150 --> 18:13.050
P-Please don't make it such a big deal...

18:13.050 --> 18:14.430
It <i>is</i> a big deal!

18:14.430 --> 18:16.320
We don't want to draw 
attention. Can we just go?

18:16.320 --> 18:17.950
Of course you can't!

18:20.240 --> 18:22.200
Go on, Karen. Say you're sorry.

18:22.530 --> 18:25.920
I'm sorry for shouting and causing a scene.

18:25.920 --> 18:30.250
You know it's a guild rule that we 
can't give out personal information!

18:30.250 --> 18:31.470
I'm sorry!

18:31.470 --> 18:35.550
It's the first time a new labyrinth has 
been discovered, so I lost my composure!

18:35.550 --> 18:39.200
Uh, as long as you'll be more 
careful in the future...

18:39.200 --> 18:41.000
You said your name is Takumi?

18:41.000 --> 18:41.510
Yes.

18:41.930 --> 18:45.360
We'll have to tell the provincial 
lord that a new labyrinth was found,

18:45.360 --> 18:47.950
and then conduct our own investigation.

18:47.950 --> 18:51.520
Can you tell me in more detail 
about how you found it?

18:51.520 --> 18:52.980
All right.

18:54.120 --> 18:57.850
So... it's called the 53rd 
labyrinth, Sazanami.

18:57.850 --> 19:01.270
We found it along the coast 
to the east of this town...

19:01.270 --> 19:02.120
Near here.

19:02.900 --> 19:05.680
There's a big reef under the water.

19:05.680 --> 19:08.000
That's where the labyrinth entrance is.

19:08.000 --> 19:09.960
What?! It's <i>that</i> close by?!

19:10.290 --> 19:12.960
Also, the entrance is underwater.

19:12.960 --> 19:15.920
So that's why it was never found before.

19:16.200 --> 19:18.000
After going through the entrance,

19:18.000 --> 19:21.890
you have to follow an underwater passage for 
about 50 meters to get to the labyrinth.

19:22.460 --> 19:24.800
There are no places to stop and breathe,

19:24.800 --> 19:27.350
so you'd have to hold your 
breath the whole way.

19:27.350 --> 19:31.400
It's probably best if you use a 
magical device to make up for that.

19:31.400 --> 19:34.670
And how did you get to such a place?

19:35.840 --> 19:40.280
<i>The mermaid bracelets would be 
too hard so explain, so I won't.</i>

19:40.590 --> 19:43.160
I just have a lot of confidence 
in my lung capacity!

19:43.470 --> 19:45.730
You're rank A, after all!

19:45.730 --> 19:48.130
I bet that's no problem for you!

19:48.130 --> 19:50.040
<i>Why are you the one looking smug?</i>

19:50.360 --> 19:52.790
Taku, we're hungry.

19:53.120 --> 19:56.970
Sorry, guys. I'm just finishing 
up. Want to go eat now?

19:56.970 --> 19:57.500
Yeah!

19:58.060 --> 20:01.010
That's all I can tell you.

20:01.010 --> 20:02.790
Okay. Thanks.

20:02.790 --> 20:06.220
You'll have to come with me to meet 
the provincial lord tomorrow.

20:07.030 --> 20:07.930
Huh?

20:07.930 --> 20:09.600
<i>So, the next day,</i>

20:09.600 --> 20:13.900
<i>I went with the guild staff to visit 
the home of the lord of Bailey.</i>

20:14.220 --> 20:17.630
It's good to meet you. 
You're Takumi, correct?

20:17.630 --> 20:21.110
I'm the provincial lord 
of Bailey, Cedric Risner.

20:21.360 --> 20:22.740
What? Risner?

20:22.740 --> 20:26.570
Stare...

20:24.130 --> 20:26.570
Oh? Hasn't Issac told you about me?

20:28.390 --> 20:30.790
A letter introducing you to 
the provincial lord of Bailey.

20:31.800 --> 20:33.870
I'm acquainted with Bailey's lord.

20:33.870 --> 20:35.830
Only that you were acquainted...

20:37.150 --> 20:38.680
Again with that...

20:38.680 --> 20:40.830
Issac is my younger brother.

20:40.830 --> 20:42.120
Your <i>brother</i>?!

20:42.120 --> 20:46.550
I suppose he kept quiet about 
it so you'd be surprised.

20:46.810 --> 20:50.550
So you're Sir Risner's older brother...

20:51.260 --> 20:56.480
<i>Man, that's confusing! They're both Risners?</i>

20:56.480 --> 21:02.120
I'm sorry. Would you mind if 
I called you "Lord Cedric"?

21:02.120 --> 21:05.420
Of course. And no need for the title.

21:05.420 --> 21:07.240
Oh, yes, I think there is!

21:07.240 --> 21:09.950
How about "Mr. Cedric" 
as a compromise, then?

21:11.330 --> 21:15.120
Alan, Elena. It's rude to point at people.

21:15.120 --> 21:16.230
Okay!

21:16.230 --> 21:17.790
Anyway, what is it?

21:18.010 --> 21:19.500
He looks like him!

21:19.500 --> 21:23.210
The knight who said we 
could kick that other guy!

21:23.480 --> 21:25.680
Ah, you mean when...

21:26.010 --> 21:28.470
I mean, you don't look 
<i>that</i> strong, y'know?! {ep3 final}

21:30.190 --> 21:32.470
The next time the Captain 
does something rude,

21:32.470 --> 21:34.370
you're welcome to send him flying.

21:34.370 --> 21:35.270
'Kay! {/ep3}

21:35.540 --> 21:37.010
Looks like him!

21:35.820 --> 21:37.010
Hey!

21:37.010 --> 21:38.100
Looks like him!

21:38.100 --> 21:42.230
Um... You're saying I look 
just like Issac, right?

21:38.680 --> 21:40.680
Looks like him!

21:40.860 --> 21:42.230
Looks like him!

21:42.580 --> 21:45.650
It has been a while since I've seen him...

21:46.040 --> 21:49.670
Has he developed a fondness for 
getting kicked by young children?!

21:49.670 --> 21:50.660
He hasn't!

21:51.020 --> 21:55.810
Come on, you guys! You gave 
Mr. Cedric the wrong idea!

21:55.810 --> 21:56.790
My brother...

21:56.790 --> 21:57.790
I-It's not like that!

21:57.790 --> 21:59.290
Can we kick him?

21:57.790 --> 21:59.290
It's more like, um...

21:59.290 --> 22:00.290
No!

22:01.710 --> 22:07.910
<i>I knew I had to clear up the 
misunderstanding to restore Issac's honor,</i>

22:03.220 --> 22:05.310
Can we kick him?

22:05.310 --> 22:06.630
My brother...

22:06.630 --> 22:09.650
It's Vau—someone else they want to kick!

22:07.910 --> 22:12.670
<i>but I couldn't just tell him it was 
Vault that they were told to kick...</i>

23:44.980 --> 23:49.990
<b>Next Time</b>

23:45.480 --> 23:49.990
<b>I Hope We Can Make Friends...</b>

23:45.910 --> 23:47.500
I hope we...

23:47.500 --> 23:49.020
...can make friends...
